     "text": [
      "ACID properties in a Database Management System (DBMS) are a\n",
      "set of four core rules—\n",
      "\n",
      "‘Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, and Durability —that guarantee\n",
      "database transactions are processed reliably and maintain data\n",
      "integrity. @ Naukri.com\n",
      "\n",
      "The Four ACID Properties\n",
      "\n",
      "« Atomicity (All or Nothing): Every transaction is treated as a single, indivisible unit.\n",
      "Either all operations inside the transaction succeed, or none of them are applied. If a\n",
      "single part fails, the entire process rolls back. €} GeeksforGeeks +2\n",
      "\n",
      "¢ Consistency (Valid State): A transaction brings the database from one valid state to\n",
      "another. It must obey all defined rules, constraints, and relationships like primary keys.\n",
      "If any rule breaks, the database rolls back the change. {8} Scribd 1\n",
      "\n",
      "+ Isolation (Independent Execution): Concurrent transactions run separately without\n",
      "interfering with each other. The intermediate state of one transaction remains invisible\n",
      "to others until it finishes. This prevents data glitches like dirty reads.\n",
      "\n",
      "@® Youtube- ByteByteGo +2\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
